To recap, we're trying to train a model to learn the vector field $v_t(x)$ that satisfies $$\frac{dx}{dt}=v_t(x)$$ which corresponds to learning a straight line path from the noise $p_1$ to the data $p_0$.

    \begin{center}
    \begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]
        % Noise Distribution
        \draw[fill=gray!20, opacity=0.5] (-3,0) circle (0.8);
        \node at (-3,1.2) {\tiny Noise $p_1$};

        % Data Distribution
        \draw[fill=blue!20, opacity=0.5] (3,0.5) ellipse (1.2 and 0.8);
        \node at (3,1.5) {\tiny Data $p_0$};

        % Vector Field Arrows
        \foreach \y in {-0.5, 0, 0.5} {
            \draw[->, thick, blue!60] (-2, \y) -- (1.5, \y + 0.3);
        }

        \node[blue] at (-0.1, 1.2) {$v_t(x) \approx \text{DiT}(x_t, t, c)$};

        % Equation
        \node at (0, -1.5) [draw, rounded corners, fill=orange!5]
            {$\mathcal{L}_{FM} = \mathbb{E}_{t, x_0, x_1} \left\| v_t(x_t) - (x_1 - x_0) \right\|^2$};
    \end{tikzpicture}
    \end{center}
